====== TP-Link EAP235-Wall v1======

The EAP235-Wall is an 802.11ac 2x2:2 Gigabit PoE+ MediaTek-based wall mount access point. Aside from the PoE+ Ethernet port that powers the device, it offers three additional gigabit ports, with the last one offering PoE passthrough. So far, **EU** and **US** versions have been spotted (differences are probably in software rather than hardware).

{{media:tplink:eap235-wall:tp-link_eap235-wall_v1.png?200|EAP235-Wall angled view}}

===== Initial Notes and Warning =====

Due to an [[https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/518|issue]] with the driver for the MT7613BE chip, 5GHz Wi-Fi is not stable in the current 21.02.0 release. A [[https://github.com/ptpt52/mt76/commit/eceab757eb708a8348e0b8d6fa860b26eec5e807|workaround]] is available. In order to have stable 5GHz Wi-Fi you need to build 21.02.0 with the patch applied. [[docs:guide-developer:toolchain:use-buildsystem|Build system usage]] has a good description of how to build OpenWrt. Just apply the patch after you did the ''git checkout v21.02.0'' using:

<code bash>
mkdir package/kernel/mt76/patches/
wget -O package/kernel/mt76/patches/002-clearPending.patch https://github.com/ptpt52/mt76/commit/eceab757eb708a8348e0b8d6fa860b26eec5e807.patch
</code>

